PRS-CS (github.com/getian107/PRScs, MIT, LICENSE here) files as patched for the bench-sim all-variant arm; they replace
the same files of the install that prscs_auto.PRSCS points at. Every change but the first is opt-in by environment
variable, so with none set PRS-CS runs its own code:
- parse_genet.py: set membership in parse_ldblk (always on; output bit-identical); PRSCS_LD_CACHE saves/loads its output;
  PRSCS_DEVICE=gpu runs the symmetrizing SVD on the GPU (max relative difference 2e-14 against scipy on a 6,922 block).
- mcmc_gtb.py: PRSCS_DEVICE=gpu runs each block's Cholesky, triangular solves and quadratic form in float64 on CuPy,
  every draw still on the host (validate_gpu.py: 5 iterations of two chains from one seed agree to 8e-15 relative);
  PRSCS_GIG=vector draws psi for all variants at once.
- gigrnd.py: gigrnd_vec, the same Devroye sampler over arrays (validate_gig.py: KS against the scalar sampler and
  scipy's exact GIG at 8 parameter sets, 1e5 draws each, all P > 0.1).
